doc cat(a, b, ...): the values shown as text, one after another.
  ```
  let n = 3
  print cat("n is ", n, ", even: ", n % 2 == 0)   // n is 3, even: false
  ```

  Each argument goes through `show`, so it can be an `int`, `str`, `bool`,
  `u8`, `[int]` or `[str]`. It builds the string in one buffer.

needs strfmt/lib strfmt/show_int strfmt/show_str strfmt/show_bool strfmt/show_char strfmt/show_ints strfmt/show_strs
syntax expr
  cat ( {xs: args} ) -> str
expand
  sb_str({each v in xs}sf_put({end}sb_new(){each v in xs}, show({v})){end})
